    "description": "### Welcome to BrunnerCTF 2026\n\nDear interns in Brunnerne Inc.™ - before starting your internship with us, here is some important introductory information, especially if you are new to CTFs\n\n### What is a CTF?\n\nA CTF (Capture The Flag) is a cybersecurity competition with challenges in areas like web exploitation, pwn, reverse engineering, cryptography, digital forensics, boot2root, and more.\n\nEach challenge hides a flag in the format `brunner{something}`, often in [1337](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leet). Submit flags to earn points.\n\n### Onboarding\n\nYou are currently in `Onboarding` - beginner-friendly challenges worth 10-40 points each. These challenges are tagged with the actual category.\n\nIf you get stuck with an `Onboarding` challenge, you can request hints on Discord via a `Hint` ticket - but always force yourself to really \"try harder\" first. No hints will be provided for other challenges.\n\n### Dynamic Scoring\n\nAll other challenges are scored *dynamically*: the more solves a challenge has, the less it is worth for everyone who has solved it. Due to this, you might see your score decrease during the CTF.\n\nChallenges start at a 1000 points and gradually decrease in score. After a specific number of solves, they reach a minimum of 100 points.\n\n### Instanced Challenges\n\nSome challenges only have a downloadable handout file. Others require you to connect to a website or server. Most of these have a \"Start Challenge\" button that starts your team's instance of that challenge. Only your team has access to this instance.\n\n### Let's Go!\n\nBefore you move on, please read the [rules](/rules) of the CTF carefully. They contain important notes on what you're allowed to and not.\n\nThen, submit the following flag:  \n`brunner{welcome_to_your_new_unpaid_internship}`\n",
